    {
      "id": 32,
      "type": "Note",
      "pos": [
        200,
        -821.4601983242662
      ],
      "size": [
        1135,
        330
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 1,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "text": ""
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "Automatic text/watermark removal with LaMa (no prompt, sampler, or denoise).\n\nEasyOCR detects text, Masks Combine Batch unions all detections, and MaskFix+ grows/cleans the mask. LaMa receives the hard cropped mask; MaskBlur+ is used only for the final paste-back seam.\n\nRequired model: big-lama.pt in the configured models/inpaint folder.\n\nThe crop uses 96px padding because LaMa normalizes it to 256x256. If detected text regions are very far apart, their combined bounding box may make each glyph too small; crop the source first or process separated regions independently."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
